---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '@/components/Section.astro';
import PageHero from '@/components/PageHero.astro';
const title = 'Privacy';
const description = 'This website sets no cookies and runs no analytics. Vekrun Personal keeps your work on your machine, Vekrun Teams on your own servers, and model providers receive only what a job sends them.';
---
<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Privacy" title="Nothing here watches you." lede="No cookies, no analytics, no trackers on this site. In the product, your work stays on machines you control, and you decide what reaches a model provider." align="left" />
  <Section padded="tight" class="pb-24">
    <div class="prose-site max-w-3xl text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="!mt-0">This website</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No cookies and no tracking. The only thing stored in your browser is your theme choice, if you change it.</li>
        <li>No analytics or advertising scripts.</li>
        <li>Fonts and search run from this site itself. Nothing is loaded from third parties.</li>
        <li>The site is hosted on GitHub Pages, so GitHub may log requests under its <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy statement</a>. Vekrun does not see those logs.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If analytics are ever added, this page will say exactly what is collected before they are turned on.</p>

      <h2>Vekrun Personal</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No Vekrun account is needed, and your work passes through no Vekrun server.</li>
        <li>Projects, jobs, Engineering Memory, logs and audit history are stored on your machine. You can delete them and remove keys at any time.</li>
        <li>Keys live in your operating system’s keychain and are kept out of logs.</li>
        <li>Usage reporting is off unless you turn it on.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Vekrun Teams</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The Coordinator, organization data store, workers, memory and audit history run on infrastructure your organization controls.</li>
        <li>Vekrun ships the software, licences, updates and support. It does not operate your servers or receive your code through them.</li>
        <li>Your organization sets access, retention and data-sharing policies, and is responsible for the servers it runs.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Model providers and connected services</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>When a job uses an external model provider, that provider receives the prompts and the code the job sends it, under your account and its terms. Local models keep that on your hardware.</li>
        <li>Before anything is sent to a provider you can see what will be sent, and your policies decide which providers are allowed.</li>
        <li>Trackers, Git hosts and monitoring services you connect receive what the actions you authorize need.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>
